{"schema_version": 2, "unit_id": "tag:02V3:statement", "parent_tag": "01UB", "chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nAssume <MATH_0002> locally of finite type. Formation of the set\n<MATHSEG_0001> is a complete intersection over <MATHSEG_0002>\ncommutes with arbitrary base change:\nFor any morphism <MATH_0003>, consider\nthe base change <MATH_0004> of <MATH_0005> and the\nprojection <MATH_0006>. Then the corresponding\nset <MATH_0007> for the morphism <MATH_0008> is equal to <MATH_0009>.\nIn particular, if <MATH_0010> is assumed flat, and locally of finite\npresentation then the same holds for the open set of points\nwhere <MATH_0011> is syntomic.\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATHSEG_0001": "$$\nT = \\{x \\in X \\mid \\mathcal{O}_{X_{f(x)}, x}\n\\text{", "MATHSEG_0002": "}\\kappa(f(x))\\}\n$$", "MATH_0003": "$g : S' \\to S$", "MATH_0004": "$f' : X' \\to S'$", "MATH_0005": "$f$", "MATH_0006": "$g' : X' \\to X$", "MATH_0007": "$T'$", "MATH_0008": "$f'$", "MATH_0009": "$T' = (g')^{-1}(T)$", "MATH_0010": "$f$", "MATH_0011": "$f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-set-points-where-fibres-lci}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "math_text_regions": [{"region_id": "math/0001", "delimiter_kind": "display-dollar", "source": "$$\nT = \\{x \\in X \\mid \\mathcal{O}_{X_{f(x)}, x}\n\\text{ is a complete intersection over }\\kappa(f(x))\\}\n$$", "source_hash": "sha256:5e822dfde8773416f77e0dcc79220c6b8c7b20d6daff974dc8bf083f3827cf3c", "source_byte_span": {"start": 156, "end": 261}, "pieces": [{"kind": "locked", "placeholder": "MATHSEG_0001"}, {"kind": "text", "slot_id": "math/0001/text/0001"}, {"kind": "locked", "placeholder": "MATHSEG_0002"}], "slots": [{"slot_id": "math/0001/text/0001", "source": " is a complete intersection over ", "command": "text